1
00:00:38,160 --> 00:00:39,477
Thank

2
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:40,877
you

3
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:47,960
so

4
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:53,839
much for watching.

5
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:22,820
Oh, oh, oh, oh

6
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:32,660
Mock? That's right.

7
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:34,020
He's my hero.

8
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:37,840
He's always laughing and
dancing to a rhythm like this.

9
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:48,740
Kuma's Life.

10
00:02:01,100 --> 00:02:05,040
Hey, Bonnie, Bonnie, Bonnie!

11
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:07,280
Come on.

12
00:02:09,480 --> 00:02:13,560
Not just Bonnie, Captain Bonnie.

13
00:02:14,900 --> 00:02:16,429
Ha, Captain, take it easy.

14
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:17,781
This is the one.

15
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:21,217
Kumachi is on that island.
What? Are you sure?

16
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:23,380
As sure as I can be!

17
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:26,933
Problem is, the place is
swarming with marines right now.

18
00:02:28,460 --> 00:02:29,290
Dad...

19
00:02:29,660 --> 00:02:31,457
Mainland Vulcan!

20
00:02:31,540 --> 00:02:32,800
Time to go!

21
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:40,580
Look out!

22
00:02:40,740 --> 00:02:42,034
It's the body pirates!

23
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:44,560
HQ said that they're a priority target!

24
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:49,160
Everywhere they go, they leave
injured children and senior citizens!

25
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:50,510
Bastards!

26
00:02:50,593 --> 00:02:52,737
They're too scared to pick on
someone who can fight back!

27
00:02:52,820 --> 00:02:55,240
Let's make these dirtbags pay! Fire!

28
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:57,220
Out of my way!

29
00:02:57,900 --> 00:02:58,840
It's yours!

30
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:04,190
Kumaji!

31
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:06,020
Come on in, it's us!

32
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:08,660
A big guy wearing black.

33
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,357
I think I just saw him
on the edge of town.

34
00:03:11,440 --> 00:03:12,270
Captain!

35
00:03:12,353 --> 00:03:13,800
There's been a Kumaji satin!

36
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:15,020
Be right there!

37
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:17,430
Which way?

38
00:03:17,513 --> 00:03:19,300
At the edge of town! Got it!

39
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:21,940
I wish I could explain, Bonnie.

40
00:03:22,260 --> 00:03:23,907
But we can't see each other.

41
00:03:25,620 --> 00:03:27,208
Please stop looking for me.

42
00:03:28,220 --> 00:03:30,060
Why wasn't he there?

43
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:31,340
Don't rush it.

44
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:34,345
Pirates like us have all
the time in the world.

45
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:40,450
That's right.

46
00:03:40,980 --> 00:03:41,810
Nika.

47
00:03:42,360 --> 00:03:44,120
I want to look for Nika, too!

48
00:03:45,180 --> 00:03:48,940
Then, when I do find Dad, I
can tell him I met his hero.

49
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:50,560
He'll be so excited.

50
00:03:53,540 --> 00:03:55,700
Meanwhile, in the east blue...

51
00:03:59,260 --> 00:04:00,460
Gum-Gum!

52
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:08,437
The upstart pirate Straw Hat
Luffy suddenly rose to prominence.

53
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:10,755
after taking down Arlong and his crew.

54
00:04:10,940 --> 00:04:11,980
All right!

55
00:04:12,140 --> 00:04:13,420
I got a real bounty!

56
00:04:16,060 --> 00:04:17,900
I'm headed out to Log Town.

57
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,200
What for?

58
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:20,974
Want me to come along?

59
00:04:21,140 --> 00:04:22,140
It's fine.

60
00:04:22,460 --> 00:04:24,989
But for the record,
who is in charge there?

61
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:26,700
Should be Captain Smoker.

62
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:28,800
Jinbei, look!

63
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:31,511
Can you guess how I know this pirate here?

64
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:34,380
Luffy is my little brother!

65
00:04:34,760 --> 00:04:35,880
Wait, he's what?

66
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:39,159
The kid who beat the Arlong
Pirates is your brother?

67
00:04:39,660 --> 00:04:42,197
Funny how things work out, huh, Dragon?

68
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:44,800
Both of our children became pirates.

69
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:48,380
This is the iron code that
all pirates must live by.

70
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:50,365
Plunder all treasure in sight!

71
00:04:50,960 --> 00:04:52,060
Plunder treasure!

72
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:53,860
Only from bad guys!

73
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:55,120
Never show mercy!

74
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:56,590
No mercy!

75
00:04:56,820 --> 00:04:57,840
But be nice!

76
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:00,180
Is this right?

77
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:01,640
You nailed it!

78
00:05:01,780 --> 00:05:04,597
I mean, I'm not an expert,
but it looks good to me.

79
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:06,100
Yes, I'm mature.

80
00:05:06,460 --> 00:05:10,357
I put some jewelry on my cheeks so
Dad can recognize me without my gems.

81
00:05:10,440 --> 00:05:13,660
Now all that's left is to get famous!

82
00:05:14,060 --> 00:05:16,589
That way he'll be able
to find me for sure!

83
00:05:19,240 --> 00:05:21,460
He'll find me. Right, Dad?

84
00:05:25,920 --> 00:05:27,040
Very unsettling.

85
00:05:27,360 --> 00:05:28,620
I'm sure it is.

86
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:32,898
But these clones and your modifications
are going to change the world.

87
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:34,255
And speaking of itch,

88
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:37,717
did you hear about the pirate who
declared war on the government?

89
00:05:37,800 --> 00:05:40,580
Shoot down that flag. Roger.

90
00:05:41,500 --> 00:05:42,330
Huh?

91
00:05:42,413 --> 00:05:44,240
The boy is Dragon Son, you say?

92
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:48,197
You'll see my memories eventually, so
there's no point in hiding it from you.

93
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:50,317
What caught my attention is that Straw Hat

94
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:52,377
fights for freedom with
the power of rubber.

95
00:05:52,460 --> 00:05:55,360
He sounds a lot like my hero. Nika.

96
00:05:56,640 --> 00:05:57,800
He does indeed.

97
00:05:58,340 --> 00:05:59,540
Here we go!

98
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:02,660
The Bomb Giant Jet Show!

99
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:09,517
My orders are to annihilate
every last one of you without

100
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:13,457
exception but i will spare your
lives in exchange for the head of

101
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:17,137
Straw Hat luffy the government
should be satisfied with his life

102
00:06:17,220 --> 00:06:20,077
alone you want us to betray our

103
00:06:20,160 --> 00:06:24,240
captain not a chance what a pity

104
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:34,957
you want someone's head
fine i'll give you one but

105
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:38,340
i can't let you have my
captains So take mine instead

106
00:06:39,260 --> 00:06:42,417
Because Luffy is the man
who will become king of

107
00:06:42,500 --> 00:06:45,877
the pirates If you truly
wish to take his place

108
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:49,117
You must be willing to
accept his agony yourself

109
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:52,100
This would be enough
to knock me unconscious

110
00:06:58,300 --> 00:07:00,820
He inspires such loyalty in his friends

111
00:07:01,560 --> 00:07:04,500
He couldn't be anyone's
son but yours, dragon

112
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:10,720
Seven warlords, report in immediately.

113
00:07:11,080 --> 00:07:12,668
Refuse and lose your title.

114
00:07:13,140 --> 00:07:14,457
That's awfully dramatic.

115
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:15,420
What happened?

116
00:07:15,740 --> 00:07:18,057
Preparations for the
execution of Porcus D.

117
00:07:18,140 --> 00:07:18,970
Ace.

118
00:07:19,053 --> 00:07:21,017
He's a standard bearer
to the new generation.

119
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:22,980
But he's a son to Whitebeard.

120
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:24,580
We expect war.

121
00:07:25,260 --> 00:07:27,620
A war with the Whitebeard pirates?

122
00:07:28,200 --> 00:07:30,140
Don't worry, I'll be there.

123
00:07:30,680 --> 00:07:32,457
Where's the rest of the food?

124
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:35,580
Bring it before I starve! Pizza!

125
00:07:36,200 --> 00:07:37,800
I'll get more pizza!

126
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:42,680
Captain, I swear they're cooking as
fast as I can! Really? Of course!

127
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:45,477
Please don't make a scene, Captain!

128
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:48,660
This will be the last
time I see you, Bonnie.

129
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:52,508
You've become quite the
pirate, haven't you?

130
00:07:54,620 --> 00:07:57,340
A pirate punched a celestial dragon!

131
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:02,860
Human shot.

132
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:06,020
Can someone attack a celestial dragon?

133
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:09,794
The whole world knows that's forbidden.

134
00:08:10,220 --> 00:08:14,560
And to do it so close to
Navy HQ, this is suicide!

135
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:24,140
It's them.

136
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:26,020
The Straw Hat Pirates.

137
00:08:30,700 --> 00:08:33,759
Are they trying to protect
a fish man and a mermaid?

138
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:40,240
What have you done, Straw Hat Luffy?

139
00:08:42,240 --> 00:08:45,000
This is an unimaginable act of rebellion.

140
00:08:46,760 --> 00:08:49,060
No one has even attempted such a thing.

141
00:08:50,340 --> 00:08:51,700
Not for centuries.

142
00:08:58,540 --> 00:09:00,520
Stand down, Pucci.

143
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:07,757
Dragon... Eva...

144
00:09:07,840 --> 00:09:10,800
Forgive me for disappearing
without a word.

145
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:24,000
I leave only two things behind as
proof that I existed in this world.

146
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:31,860
Lonnie, and the future of
this boy, Straw Hat Luffy.

147
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:44,560
I couldn't save any of them.

148
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:46,860
What's wrong with me?

149
00:09:49,740 --> 00:09:53,720
Nothing, but this is how
harsh the new world will be.

150
00:09:55,520 --> 00:09:59,226
You and your friends aren't ready
for it You must grow stronger

151
00:10:00,320 --> 00:10:02,000
And when the time comes

152
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:05,520
Someday You'll save this world

153
00:10:12,540 --> 00:10:17,420
A self-destruct switch Do you
really fear Kuma that much?

154
00:10:17,580 --> 00:10:21,337
You did turn him into a deadly
human weapon Did you not?

155
00:10:21,420 --> 00:10:23,891
You're at the top of his authority ladder.

156
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:29,580
And if he goes berserk when we're out of
command range, who will stop him and how?

157
00:10:29,720 --> 00:10:30,640
I don't!

158
00:10:30,940 --> 00:10:34,540
Cease your insolence,
you paltry hired hand.

159
00:10:34,820 --> 00:10:39,080
All right, I'll do as you ask, but
please let him keep some free will.

160
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:43,477
I've invented a brain circuit that
can toggle between personality modes.

161
00:10:43,560 --> 00:10:45,777
It will be easy to install,
I promise you just...

162
00:10:45,860 --> 00:10:48,213
I gave you a very clear order, Vegapunk.

163
00:10:48,420 --> 00:10:51,280
Destroy every trace of his free will.

164
00:10:51,420 --> 00:10:53,000
We're both men of science.

165
00:10:53,260 --> 00:10:54,460
You can't fool me.

166
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:56,856
But what will become of his daughter?

167
00:10:57,020 --> 00:10:57,960
What of Bonnie?

168
00:10:58,220 --> 00:11:00,040
He will never see her again!

169
00:11:04,940 --> 00:11:07,360
Thank you for trying, Vigipunk.

170
00:11:08,660 --> 00:11:11,020
You didn't hear all of that, did you?

171
00:11:12,500 --> 00:11:15,460
Turns out a scientist gave
me superhuman hearing.

172
00:11:25,660 --> 00:11:28,940
All right, today's the day
you lose your free will.

173
00:11:29,340 --> 00:11:33,540
I've only known you for two years,
but we've had some good times.

174
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:35,540
We have.

175
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:40,417
Seems your first mission will be a large-scale
fight against the Whitebeard pilots.

176
00:11:40,500 --> 00:11:43,618
The Navy's requesting a
massive deployment of clones.

177
00:11:44,420 --> 00:11:48,420
If you wouldn't mind, could you
program one more mission after that?

178
00:11:49,620 --> 00:11:52,440
You want to guard the Strawhead's ship?

179
00:11:52,900 --> 00:11:54,877
Until one of his crewmates comes back.

180
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:56,717
I want to help them protect their home.

181
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:58,077
It's a shame.

182
00:11:58,160 --> 00:12:00,577
I wish that I could watch
their journey to the end?

183
00:12:00,660 --> 00:12:04,180
What is it that you expect from that boy?

184
00:12:04,500 --> 00:12:06,197
His actions move my soul.

185
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:08,117
I don't know how else to put it.

186
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:10,500
He's a legend come to life.

187
00:12:11,740 --> 00:12:14,137
I know Nika is just an old folk tale.

188
00:12:14,220 --> 00:12:17,857
But I told Bonnie that there's a warrior
who moves to the rhythm of liberation.

189
00:12:17,940 --> 00:12:19,700
and brings smiles to all.

190
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:24,308
If there really is a hero who
can change the world like Nika?

191
00:12:25,560 --> 00:12:28,360
I think it'll be Straw Hat.

192
00:12:28,900 --> 00:12:31,220
A revolutionary betting on a pirate?

193
00:12:32,080 --> 00:12:34,520
You've chosen quite the dark horse.

194
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:36,860
What a contradiction.

195
00:12:37,260 --> 00:12:38,731
Proof you're still human.

196
00:12:38,960 --> 00:12:41,920
Now, about that sample for my research.

197
00:12:42,400 --> 00:12:43,980
We had a deal, right?

198
00:12:45,940 --> 00:12:48,777
Then you push your memories
into a paw like that.

199
00:12:48,860 --> 00:12:49,977
Do you forget them?

200
00:12:50,060 --> 00:12:54,020
No, it's like a copy, but it will
vanish after someone touches it.

201
00:12:54,700 --> 00:12:55,720
Fine with me.

202
00:12:55,980 --> 00:12:58,333
I devised a method to study it remotely.

203
00:12:58,600 --> 00:12:59,776
Keep it right there.

204
00:13:00,020 --> 00:13:01,960
Now, let's get this over with.

205
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:04,860
Purely clinical, I am a scientist.

206
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:09,680
I see.

207
00:13:10,640 --> 00:13:12,440
So this is my life.

208
00:13:16,280 --> 00:13:19,257
I wonder how many people I've
troubled through the years.

209
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:20,399
Troubled, you say?

210
00:13:20,740 --> 00:13:23,020
Why, to live is to trouble others.

211
00:14:06,820 --> 00:14:10,020
By the way, what age
did you become a slave?

212
00:14:10,980 --> 00:14:12,240
When I was four.

213
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:13,660
Same as me!

214
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:15,670
Kumachi!

215
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:20,769
I'm the eldest here by four years, so
that means it's my job to keep you fed!

216
00:14:23,120 --> 00:14:23,950
Kumaji!

217
00:14:28,660 --> 00:14:29,577
That's enough!

218
00:14:29,660 --> 00:14:30,601
Let's sell them!

219
00:14:38,540 --> 00:14:39,700
Kumaji! Kumaji!

220
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:52,950
Kumachi!

221
00:14:56,960 --> 00:14:58,860
I'm full!

222
00:14:59,380 --> 00:15:00,920
I'm full!

223
00:15:01,640 --> 00:15:03,620
I'm full!

224
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:11,880
I'm so happy!

225
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:14,717
Kumachi...

226
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:19,080
I'll always, always, love you.

227
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:37,060
Don't worry, Jenny.

228
00:15:38,140 --> 00:15:40,480
I'll raise your daughter as my home.

229
00:15:41,860 --> 00:15:42,690
Daddy!

230
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:45,190
Dad?

231
00:15:46,740 --> 00:15:47,570
Dad?

232
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:56,460
Those little jerks!

233
00:15:57,240 --> 00:15:59,828
They were making fun
of my face rocks again.

234
00:16:00,180 --> 00:16:02,180
I wish I could throw them at them.

235
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:03,980
Guess they are kind of ugly.

236
00:16:04,460 --> 00:16:05,872
But I'm stuck with them.

237
00:16:06,100 --> 00:16:07,159
They're permanent.

238
00:16:07,460 --> 00:16:09,342
I'm going to be honest with you.

239
00:16:09,760 --> 00:16:13,300
Your daughter has five
years to live at most.

240
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:17,581
She would be beating the odds just
to make it to her 10th birthday.

241
00:16:19,220 --> 00:16:21,060
I'm afraid your mother's dead.

242
00:16:21,860 --> 00:16:24,120
But that means she's in heaven now.

243
00:16:26,140 --> 00:16:27,640
You'll be okay, Kuma.

244
00:16:28,040 --> 00:16:28,980
You're strong.

245
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:30,871
You just have to survive.

246
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:32,900
Don't give up. Why?

247
00:16:33,300 --> 00:16:35,780
I think I'd be better off dead, too.

248
00:16:36,400 --> 00:16:40,500
The warrior of liberation will
save you. Have faith. He'll come.

249
00:16:40,700 --> 00:16:42,280
Who is that?

250
00:16:45,240 --> 00:16:47,540
I can't take it anymore.

251
00:16:47,980 --> 00:16:49,440
I'd rather die!

252
00:16:50,020 --> 00:16:52,100
I can't lose anyone else!

253
00:16:52,480 --> 00:16:55,080
I won't lose anyone else!

254
00:17:02,540 --> 00:17:03,380
Mock?

255
00:17:03,900 --> 00:17:04,730
That's right.

256
00:17:05,040 --> 00:17:06,060
He's my hero.

257
00:17:06,660 --> 00:17:09,131
Does that mean he'll come and free me too?

258
00:17:14,220 --> 00:17:17,044
A mass of pain and suffering
won't just go away.

259
00:17:17,140 --> 00:17:19,820
In the end, someone has to accept it.

260
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:29,560
Never forget, those hands
can do more than pray.

261
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:31,722
They're the hands of liberation!

262
00:17:40,700 --> 00:17:41,530
Thank you.

263
00:17:44,900 --> 00:17:49,900
If you can help Bonnie get well,
then I'll happily accept any fate.

264
00:17:50,780 --> 00:17:52,480
Any fate at all.

265
00:17:54,220 --> 00:17:56,420
Nika, the Sun God.

266
00:17:56,780 --> 00:17:59,717
He'll show up and deliver
us all to freedom one day.

267
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:03,240
He'll take you to the sea,
beneath the free skies.

268
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:05,820
Are you sure? Of course.

269
00:18:06,100 --> 00:18:07,120
He's no joke.

270
00:18:07,620 --> 00:18:10,197
My disease will be all gone in a year.

271
00:18:10,280 --> 00:18:12,045
Then I can finally go outside!

272
00:18:12,360 --> 00:18:14,717
When I pick you up, we'll take to the sea.

273
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:17,840
From there, it's an endless
horizon. Can't wait!

274
00:18:18,100 --> 00:18:20,041
I want to go all kinds of places!

275
00:18:28,100 --> 00:18:28,930
Bonnie.

276
00:18:31,280 --> 00:18:34,620
Ever since I was young, I've had a dream.

277
00:18:35,260 --> 00:18:37,217
I've always wanted to be a hero.

278
00:18:37,300 --> 00:18:41,660
Someone who could save the downtrodden
and free people from suffering.

279
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:01,130
Kuma!

280
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:03,020
Kuma-chi!

281
00:19:07,360 --> 00:19:08,460
Kuma.

282
00:19:09,280 --> 00:19:10,380
Kuma!

283
00:19:13,660 --> 00:19:15,060
Kuma-chi!

284
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:24,040
I'll cure her!

285
00:19:28,480 --> 00:19:30,640
Daddy, you're home!

286
00:19:31,040 --> 00:19:32,120
I'm so glad.

287
00:19:37,820 --> 00:19:38,960
Thank you.

288
00:19:52,060 --> 00:19:55,020
Yes, to live is to trouble others.

289
00:19:57,680 --> 00:20:01,180
Your death will trouble
everyone who loves you.

290
00:20:01,560 --> 00:20:03,940
It's proof of a life they lived.

291
00:20:05,920 --> 00:20:10,417
I tell you, Kuma, you are a hero.

292
00:20:10,500 --> 00:20:11,777
You're Bonnie's hero.

293
00:20:11,860 --> 00:20:14,200
You're everyone's hero.

294
00:20:15,580 --> 00:20:17,060
You're too kind, Vang.

295
00:20:17,580 --> 00:20:18,410
Vegapunk.

296
00:20:21,040 --> 00:20:22,220
I know.

297
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:23,560
I will.

298
00:20:26,540 --> 00:20:27,420
Mock?

299
00:20:28,100 --> 00:20:29,240
That's right.

300
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:30,380
He's my hero.

301
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:34,640
Does that mean he'll
come and free me, too?

302
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:38,300
Of course you will.

303
00:20:51,980 --> 00:20:54,940
Thank you, Vegapunk, for saving Bonnie.

304
00:20:58,660 --> 00:21:00,817
Could you pass on a message for me?

305
00:21:00,900 --> 00:21:02,520
The next time you see her!

306
00:21:08,180 --> 00:21:09,010
Tell her!

307
00:21:13,980 --> 00:21:15,360
Happy 10th birthday.

308
00:21:24,940 --> 00:21:27,337
Oh, I'll be home to me.

309
00:21:27,420 --> 00:21:29,280
I should go to my house.

310
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:36,120
No one cannot be my hair.

311
00:21:36,760 --> 00:21:40,160
The voice of my voice is me.

312
00:21:41,760 --> 00:21:43,584
How long should I take my hand?

313
00:21:43,860 --> 00:21:46,460
I can't see the next one.

314
00:21:46,840 --> 00:21:47,717
Then move me.
